<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jemmapes (department)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jemmapes was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of the French Republic and Empire, created in 1795 from the County of Hainaut and neighbouring lands after the annexation of the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. Named after the French victory at Jemappes in 1792, it had its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fall in 1814 it became the province of Hainaut, under the Netherlands and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>.</p></div>
